{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23 makes the driver's pre-cancellation contact obligation conjunctive: before cancelling for no-show the driver must have sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call. The trip record's own derived contact check reports message_count 0 and obligation_met false, so the message limb fails outright and the 5.00 SGD fee must be voided with a FULL_REFUND of the fee charged and no driver compensation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log for this trip carries exactly one entry, and it is the rider's own message 'Coming down now, sorry', sent at 12:21:50 and delivered at 12:21:53 — forty seconds AFTER the driver cancelled at 12:21:10. There is no driver message at any point in the log, before or after the cancellation, so nothing in the record can satisfy the message limb of POL-NS-23.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own account is 'I called two times, no answer.' That asserts calls and nothing else: it does not claim, and the record nowhere shows, that any in-app message was ever sent to the rider. The two in-app calls at 12:17:55 and 12:19:40 (unanswered, 20 s and 18 s) establish the call limb of POL-NS-23 and only the call limb.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's admission that his phone was on silent explains only why the two calls rang out; it does not touch the separate requirement that the driver also message him in the app. POL-NS-23 is conjunctive — a ringing call is not a message — and on this record the rider was left with no in-app notice of where the driver was waiting or that he was about to be cancelled on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider sent 'Coming down now, sorry' forty seconds after the driver cancelled, which shows he was responding and on his way down rather than lost to the trip. A single in-app message from the driver, which POL-NS-23 requires and which costs nothing, would have reached him before the cancellation instead of after it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Candidly, the arrival and wait prerequisites are met on this record: auto-arrival at 12:15:30 is corroborated by the GPS trace (nearest fix 3.07 m from the pickup point at 6 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius), and cancellation at 12:21:10 is 340 s after arrival — past the 300 s free wait. The fee therefore stands or falls on the contact obligation in POL-NS-23 alone, and there it falls.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.seconds_from_start_to_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Every fact POL-NS-23 needs is carried by COMPLETE evidence at weight 1.0 — the trip record and the chat log — so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged and no question is left open for a human. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and no fraud flag is recorded on either profile, so under POL-NS-26 the AI ruling on this no-show is final and the refund issues without escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053", "EV-FARE-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The payments ledger records exactly 5.00 SGD charged as the cancellation fee, with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the ledger's own money block puts refund_if_voided_sgd at 5.00. The remedy the record supports is therefore FULL_REFUND of 5.00 SGD — the whole contested amount returned — with no driver compensation, which is precisely what POL-NS-23 prescribes when the contact obligation is unmet.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.refund_if_voided_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat no-show referral arises under POL-NS-25: the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter at all, and the fee cannot stand, so this trip cannot be counted toward the threshold of 3. There is nothing on this record to flag the rider's account for review.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-25"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
